---
import CourseLayout from "../layouts/CourseLayout.astro";
import AcademyMark from "../components/AcademyMark.astro";
import AssessmentSummary from "../components/AssessmentSummary.astro";
import {learningOutcomes,weeks} from "../data/curriculum";
import {withBase} from "astro-theme-university/url";
import {courseMeta} from "../course-config";
import "../styles/demonstration.css";
---
<CourseLayout title={courseMeta.title} description={courseMeta.description} home>
<section class="academy-hero">
 <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">SLOP4408 · THE ACADEMY OF IMPOSSIBLE SKILLS</p><h1>MASTER<br class="hero-break"/>MIND<span>Learn the art<br/>of the impossible.</span></h1><p class="hero-description">Notice what others miss. Understand how things work. Recover what seems unreachable.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={withBase("/academy/")}>Enter the academy <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button ghost" href={withBase("/lectures/")}>Explore the course</a></div><p class="hero-caption">An original, playable Slop University course.<br/>Twelve weeks of extraordinary skills.</p></div>
 <div class="academy-illustration"><AcademyMark/><div class="art-caption"><span>01 / THE TRAINING GROUND</span><span>EST. 2027</span></div></div>
</section>
<div class="course-ribbon"><span>THIRD-PERSON EXPLORATION</span><span>12 INTERACTIVE LABS</span><span>ONE IMPOSSIBLE RECOVERY</span></div>
<section class="manifesto section-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">CURIOSITY IS THE ENTRY REQUIREMENT</p><h2>The skills you've<br/>always wondered about.</h2></div><div><p class="large-copy">How do you remember a room? Understand a mechanism? Trace a digital contradiction? Get a team through a problem that keeps changing?</p><p>Learn through original training equipment, navigable spaces and people with different information. Make a prediction. Try it. See what happens. Then use the skill somewhere new.</p><p>For fourth-year students drawn to puzzles, systems and collaborative problem-solving. No programming or security background is needed.</p></div></section>
<section class="demo-library-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE DEMONSTRATION STUDIO</p><h2>Watch the thinking.<br/>Then take the controls.</h2><p>See a coach work through a complete example in the 3D academy. Pause at a decision, inspect the apparatus and try it yourself. Every lab and assessment has its own different scenario and finished sample submission.</p></div><div><h3>Begin with a front-row seat.</h3><p>Sixteen guided experiences, with chapter controls, clear explanations and feedback shaped by your actual attempts.</p><a class="button primary" href={withBase("/demonstrations/")}>Explore the worked examples ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="capability-index"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR SEMESTER / TWELVE CAPABILITIES</p><h2>Every week changes what you can do.</h2><div class="skill-rows">{weeks.map(w=><a href={withBase("/sessions/week-"+String(w.week).padStart(2,"0")+"/")}><span class="skill-number">{String(w.week).padStart(2,"0")}</span><span><strong>{w.title}</strong><small>{w.skill}</small></span><span class="skill-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div></section>
<section class="mission-feature"><div><p class="eyebrow">FINAL MISSION / OPERATION LAST LIGHT</p><h2>Meridian is going dark.<br/>The archive must survive.</h2><p>A failed support system. Contradictory copies. Six areas of a research station, and four roles with different information.</p><p>Repair the equipment, verify the archive, reach an agreement and carry out a recovery you can defend. Everything you learned has a job to do.</p><a class="button primary" href={withBase("/operation/")}>Explore the final mission ↗</a></div><div class="mission-coordinate" aria-hidden="true"><span>MERIDIAN<br/>STATION</span><b>27</b><small>ARCHIVE INTEGRITY / UNKNOWN<br/>RECOVERY TEAM / REQUESTED</small></div></section>
<div class="section-grid"><section><p class="eyebrow">A COURSE YOU CAN ACTUALLY FOLLOW</p><h2>Learn. Try. Transfer.</h2><p>Monday: one-hour briefing. Friday: two-hour lab. Around three further hours for preparation and assessment.</p><p>22 February–28 May 2027, with a 5–18 April break. Every lab offers campus and browser routes. Remote teams can share a screen and rotate control; solo students can switch roles.</p><a href={withBase("/sessions/week-01/")}>Try the observation lab →</a></section><section><p class="eyebrow">ASSESSMENT / 100%</p><h2>Show what you can do.</h2><AssessmentSummary/><p class="small">Practical evidence, transfer, diagnosis and explanation. Game endings do not determine academic marks.</p></section></div>
<section><p class="eyebrow">WHAT YOU LEAVE WITH</p><ol class="outcome-list">{learningOutcomes.map(o=><li><span>{o.id}</span><div><strong>{o.title}</strong><span>{o.description}</span></div></li>)}</ol></section>
<div class="section-grid"><section><h2>Three instructors.<br/>Very different questions.</h2><p>Mara Voss asks how it works. Iona Vale asks what supports the claim. Sol Renn asks whether the next person can act on your instructions.</p><a href={withBase("/people/")}>Meet the teaching team ↗</a></section><section><h2>Start anywhere.</h2><p>Every briefing, lab, assessment and sample is open. Your skills passport saves locally, with exports you can keep. Accessible controls and printable teaching materials accompany the 3D experience.</p><a href={withBase("/policies/")}>Access, collaboration and course policies ↗</a></section></div>
</CourseLayout>
